# Mission plan

## Objectives

1. Intake a multi-part document (template **or** given structure) under a folder
   registered in **`.sedea/documentation-management.yaml`**.
2. Produce an approved **master plan** — overview of document sections and part
   delivery order. Unlike **Author Simple Document**, do **not** plan and render
   the entire document in one pass.
3. Deliver each part via a **part-planner** child lane that **spawns** the
   **author** child for that part. Plan revisions flow **planner → author**
   (not via Squad Leader rebroadcast). After authoring, the author reviews the
   part conversation for SoT alterations and collects per-change approvals into
   the SoT changes follow-up document. The structure of each part plan is
   defined during that part’s planning session. The **SoT changes follow-up
   document** (ops docs) records *proposed* SoT edits for a later **`refresh
   source of truth`** dispatch. It is **not**
   `<localPath>/source-of-truth/CHANGELOG.md` (audit of completed SoT writes).
   When consulting SoT while authoring a part, do **not** treat
   **`CHANGELOG.md`** as authoritative unless the user explicitly names it and
   explains how to use it (rule **20** § *Change log*).
4. Between parts, when the user requests it, spawn a **gap-analyzer** to detect
   contradictions or misinterpretations across authored parts; when gaps are
   found, the **gap-analyzer** spawns **gap-closer** on its lane (nested spawn).
   After each analyzer/closer cycle, the Squad Leader offers **another gap
   analysis run** — multiple passes often surface different issues.
5. Keep Squad Leader / master-plan standing options available for the whole
   active dispatch: **Generate Content**, **Sync documents**, **Export PDF**,
   continue part delivery, request gap analysis, and finish/approve content.
   After §2 folder bind, **every** Squad Leader structured-choice modal includes
   **`sync-documents`** so GDrive edits can bisync into the local folder without
   waiting for the §5 standing gate alone (§5a).
6. Support long-running authoring (hours, days, or weeks) with repeatable sync
   and content-generation passes until all parts are authored and the user
   approves the content.
7. **PDF export (Squad Leader):** On **user request**, offer the same PDF export
   modes as Author Simple Document (`documentation-folder-sync` |
   `operations-result` | `skip`), then spawn Convert Document **`pdf-converter`**.
   Do **not** auto-export after each part. Never replace the source document.
8. Close the dispatch with an explicit Squad Leader
   **`mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution`** when the pass is complete,
   partial, or abandoned.

## Squad operations (multi-part document delivery)

This mission is **document delivery**, not hosting-repo three-lane PR shipping.
Skills live under **`missions/author-multi-part-document/skills/`** unless noted.
Sync and PDF conversion reuse Author Simple Document / Convert Document contracts.

| Role | Lane | `execution` | Spawns / owns | Does not |
|------|------|-------------|---------------|----------|
| **Squad Leader / Master Plan agent** | Dispatch leader | — | part-planner, gap-analyzer, content-generator; sync (file-synchronizer); **PDF export gate + pdf-converter** | Spawn **author** on the happy path (part-planner owns that); spawn **gap-closer** on the happy path (gap-analyzer owns that); resolve dispatch from a child lane |
| **Part planner** | Child | `spawned` | **author** (after part-plan approval); plan-revision notify to author | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution`; requiring Squad Leader to re-spawn author for plan revisions |
| **Author** | Child | `spawned` (by part-planner) | SoT conversation review + SoT follow-up collection | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution`; spawning other parts |
| **Gap analyzer** | Child | `spawned` | **gap-closer** (when `gapsFound: true`) | Spawn gap-closer on happy path; resolve dispatch |
| **Gap closer** | Child | `spawned` (by gap-analyzer) | — | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution`; terminal to gap-analyzer parent only |
| **Content generator** | Child | `spawned` | — | `mission_control_propose_dispatch_resolution` |
| **File synchronizer** | Child | `spawned` | — | Same conflict contract as Author Simple Document |
| **PDF converter** | Child | `spawned` | Convert Document `pdf-converter` | Resolve dispatch; overwrite source |

**Dispatch display refresh (Squad Leader).** When dispatch scope is readable
(matched command phrase, folder slug, document title), call MCP
**`mission_control_update_dispatch_display`** with non-empty **`dispatchTitle`**
